Third-party components
----------------------

The desktop applications carry a copy of MariaDB, which is distributed under the
GNU General Public License version 2. It is included unmodified and is executed
as a separate program; the applications communicate with it over a socket.

The server carries the code it uses to read Transact-SQL in
orchestrator/lib/sqlserver, which is the only third-party source held in this
repository rather than fetched by a package manager. Three licences apply to it
and all three are permissive:

  * The parsing engine is BSD 3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2012-2023 The ANTLR
    Project, taken from github.com/antlr4-go/antlr/v4 v4.13.1. One line of it was
    changed, replacing golang.org/x/exp/slices with the standard library's
    slices. See lib/sqlserver/antlr/LICENSE.

  * The generated parser is BSD 3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2025 Bytebase, taken from
    github.com/bytebase/parser at commit 57b6ef7a2640. See
    lib/sqlserver/tsql/LICENSE.bytebase.

  * The grammar it is generated from (TSqlLexer.g4, TSqlParser.g4) is MIT, from
    the antlr/grammars-v4 project, with five copyright holders named in the file
    itself. See lib/sqlserver/tsql/LICENSE.grammar.

All three require their notices to be kept with the code, which is why those
files sit beside it and must not be removed. None of them imposes any obligation
on the rest of this work.

Every other dependency and its licence is listed by the package manager of the
part that uses it: go.mod for the server, package.json for the front ends, and
Cargo.toml for the desktop shells and the inference node.
